    <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">Projects</h2>
    <p>Atomdrift is the first open-source platform for AI-based malware
    detection. The tools form a pipeline: stng pulls strings, cleave
    decomposes binaries and source into structured capabilities, and
    litmus runs open-source ML models like azoth — the first
    open-source AI model for general malware detection — against that
    output. All Apache 2.0, Rust &amp; Go, developed on
    <a href="https://codeberg.org/atomdrift" target="_blank">Codeberg</a>.
    Released versions are current through 2026-04-10.</p>

